          }
        ],
        "answer": "",
        "alternateAnswers": [],
        "explanation": "First, find the points of intersection of y = x² and y = x.\nx² = x\nx² - x = 0\nx(x - 1) = 0\nSo, x = 0 and x = 1 are the intersection points.\nBetween x = 0 and x = 1, the line y = x is above the parabola y = x².\nArea A = ∫₀¹ (x - x²) dx\nA = [x²/2 - x³/3]₀¹\nA = (1²/2 - 1³/3) - (0²/2 - 0³/3)\nA = (1/2 - 1/3) - 0",
        "hint": "",
