            "explanation": ""
          },
          {
            "letter": "C",
            "text": "$8\\sqrt{3}/3$ sq. units",
            "isCorrect": false,
            "index": 2,
            "imageUrl": "",
            "explanation": ""
          },
          {
            "letter": "D",
            "text": "$16\\sqrt{3}/3$ sq. units",
            "isCorrect": false,
            "index": 3,
            "imageUrl": "",
            "explanation": ""
          }
        ],
        "answer": "",
        "alternateAnswers": [],
        "explanation": "The parabola is $y^2 = 4x$, so $y = \\pm 2\\sqrt{x}$. The region is symmetric about the x-axis.\nWe need to find the area from $x=0$ to $x=3$.\nArea $= 2 \\int_0^3 y \\, dx = 2 \\int_0^3 2\\sqrt{x} \\, dx = 4 \\int_0^3 x^{1/2} \\, dx$\n$= 4 \\left[ \\frac{x^{3/2}}{3/2} \\right]_0^3 = 4 \\times \\frac{2}{3} \\left[ x^{3/2} \\right]_0^3$\n$= \\frac{8}{3} [ (3)^{3/2} - (0)^{3/2} ] = \\frac{8}{3} [ 3\\sqrt{3} - 0 ] = 8\\sqrt{3}$ sq. units.",
        "hint": "",
        "marks": 1,
        "negativeMark": 0,
        "negativeMarking": false,
        "imageUrl": "",
