      {
        "id": "q-1789303481795-6017f",
        "order": 19,
        "question": "The area (in square units) bounded by the parabola $y^2 = 4x$ and the line $x=1$ is:",
        "type": "mcq",
        "options": [
          {
            "letter": "A",
            "text": "$\\frac{4}{3}$",
            "isCorrect": false,
            "index": 0,
            "imageUrl": "",
            "explanation": ""
          },
          {
            "letter": "B",
            "text": "$\\frac{8}{3}$",
            "isCorrect": true,
            "index": 1,
            "imageUrl": "",
            "explanation": ""
          },
          {
            "letter": "C",
            "text": "$\\frac{16}{3}$",
            "isCorrect": false,
            "index": 2,
            "imageUrl": "",
            "explanation": ""
          },
          {
            "letter": "D",
            "text": "$\\frac{2}{3}$",
            "isCorrect": false,
            "index": 3,
            "imageUrl": "",
            "explanation": ""
          }
        ],
        "answer": "",
        "alternateAnswers": [],
        "explanation": "The equation of the parabola is $y^2 = 4x$, which is symmetric about the x-axis. We can write $y = \\pm 2\\sqrt{x}$.\nThe line is $x=1$.\nThe region is bounded by the parabola from $x=0$ to $x=1$.\nThe total area is twice the area above the x-axis (since the parabola is symmetric).\nArea $A = 2 \\int_0^1 y \\, dx = 2 \\int_0^1 2\\sqrt{x} \\, dx$\n$A = 4 \\int_0^1 x^{1/2} \\, dx$\nUsing the power rule for integration, $\\int x^n \\, dx = \\frac{x^{n+1}}{n+1}$:\n$A = 4 \\left[ \\frac{x^{1/2+1}}{1/2+1} \\right]_0^1 = 4 \\left[ \\frac{x^{3/2}}{3/2} \\right]_0^1$\n$A = 4 \\left[ \\frac{2}{3} x^{3/2} \\right]_0^1$\nNow, apply the limits of integration:\n$A = 4 \\left( \\frac{2}{3} (1)^{3/2} - \\frac{2}{3} (0)^{3/2} \\right)$\n$A = 4 \\left( \\frac{2}{3} - 0 \\right) = 4 \\times \\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{8}{3}$ square units.",
        "hint": "",
        "marks": 1,
        "negativeMark": 0,
        "negativeMarking": false,
        "imageUrl": "",
