      {
        "id": "q-1789303481795-844ba",
        "order": 20,
        "question": "The value of the definite integral $\\int_0^{\\pi/2} \\frac{\\sin x}{\\sin x + \\cos x} \\, dx$ is:",
        "type": "mcq",
        "options": [
          {
            "letter": "A",
            "text": "$\\pi$",
            "isCorrect": false,
            "index": 0,
            "imageUrl": "",
            "explanation": ""
          },
          {
            "letter": "B",
            "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{4}$",
            "isCorrect": true,
            "index": 1,
            "imageUrl": "",
            "explanation": ""
          },
          {
            "letter": "C",
            "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$",
            "isCorrect": false,
            "index": 2,
            "imageUrl": "",
            "explanation": ""
          },
          {
            "letter": "D",
            "text": "$0$",
            "isCorrect": false,
            "index": 3,
            "imageUrl": "",
            "explanation": ""
          }
        ],
        "answer": "",
        "alternateAnswers": [],
        "explanation": "Let $I = \\int_0^{\\pi/2} \\frac{\\sin x}{\\sin x + \\cos x} \\, dx$.\nUsing the property of definite integrals: $\\int_0^a f(x) \\, dx = \\int_0^a f(a-x) \\, dx$.\nHere, $a = \\pi/2$.\nSo, $I = \\int_0^{\\pi/2} \\frac{\\sin(\\pi/2 - x)}{\\sin(\\pi/2 - x) + \\cos(\\pi/2 - x)} \\, dx$\n$I = \\int_0^{\\pi/2} \\frac{\\cos x}{\\cos x + \\sin x} \\, dx$ (Since $\\sin(\\pi/2 - x) = \\cos x$ and $\\cos(\\pi/2 - x) = \\sin x$)\nNow, add the original integral and this new integral:\n$I + I = \\int_0^{\\pi/2} \\frac{\\sin x}{\\sin x + \\cos x} \\, dx + \\int_0^{\\pi/2} \\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x + \\cos x} \\, dx$\n$2I = \\int_0^{\\pi/2} \\frac{\\sin x + \\cos x}{\\sin x + \\cos x} \\, dx$\n$2I = \\int_0^{\\pi/2} 1 \\, dx$\n$2I = [x]_0^{\\pi/2}$\n$2I = \\frac{\\pi}{2} - 0$\n$2I = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$\n$I = \\frac{\\pi}{4}$.",
        "hint": "",
        "marks": 1,
        "negativeMark": 0,
        "negativeMarking": false,
        "imageUrl": "",
        "subject": "isc12-maths",
        "difficulty": "easy",
        "hasError": false
