        "answer": "",
        "alternateAnswers": [],
        "explanation": "Let $r$ be the radius of the sphere and $S$ be its surface area.\nGiven $\\frac{dr}{dt} = 0.2 \\, \\text{cm/s}$.\nThe formula for the surface area of a sphere is $S = 4\\pi r^2$.\nWe need to find $\\frac{dS}{dt}$.\nDifferentiate $S$ with respect to $t$:\n$\\frac{dS}{dt} = \\frac{d}{dt}(4\\pi r^2) = 4\\pi (2r) \\frac{dr}{dt}$\n$\\frac{dS}{dt} = 8\\pi r \\frac{dr}{dt}$\nSubstitute the given values: $r = 10 \\, \\text{cm}$ and $\\frac{dr}{dt} = 0.2 \\, \\text$",
